text.section:
This chapter does not apply to:

Insurance written through the Virginia Workers' Compensation Plan pursuant to Chapter 20 (§ 38.2-2000 et seq.) of this title;


Insurance on a specific risk as provided in § 38.2-1920;


Reinsurance, other than joint reinsurance, to the extent stated in § 38.2-1915;


Life insurance as defined in § 38.2-102;


Annuities as defined in §§ 38.2-106 and 38.2-107;


Accident and sickness insurance as defined in § 38.2-109;


Title insurance as defined in § 38.2-123;


Insurance of vessels or craft used primarily in a trade or business, their cargoes, marine builders' risks and marine protection and indemnity;


Insurance against loss of or damage to hulls of aircraft, including their accessories and equipment, or against liability, other than workers' compensation and employers' liability, arising out of the ownership, maintenance or use of aircraft;


Insurance written through the Virginia Automobile Insurance Plan. However, § 38.2-1905 shall apply to insurance written through the Plan;


Insurance provided pursuant to Chapter 27 (§ 38.2-2700 et seq.);


Home protection contracts as defined by § 38.2-2600 and their rates until such time as the Commission determines there is sufficient competition in the industry as provided by § 38.2-2608.
